SUMMARY:Sam Dalrymple | Shattered Lands: Five Partitions and the Making o
 f Modern Asia
DESCRIPTION:Sam Dalrymple discusses his new book\, Shattered Lands | Five
  Partitions and the Making of Modern Asia\, a bold and sweeping history 
 of modern South Asia\, told through the five partitions that reshaped it
 . Sam Dalrymple is a historian\, filmmaker\, and cofounder of Project Da
 staan\, a peace-building initiative that reconnects refugees displaced b
 y the 1947 partition of India. He graduated from the University of Oxfor
 d as a Persian and Sanskrit scholar\, and lives in Delhi.\nhttps://www.p
 rinceton.edu/events/2026/sam-dalrymple-shattered-lands-five-partitions-a
 nd-making-modern-asia
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/sam-dalrymple-shattered-lands-f
 ive-partitions-and-making-modern-asia
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
